+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+When a GraphHelm-bound session ends, the `SessionEnd` hook posts an `agent_session_ended`
+signal to the Runtime naming its actor in `X-GraphHelm-Actor` (`<host>-session-<id>`), but the
+end request carries no host session id. The Runtime already reads an optional
+`X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session` declaration on signal requests and persists it with the actor
+presence record (`apps/cli/src/commands/serve/mod.rs`, #1057); because the hook never sends it,
+every presence record created from these ends lacks the session id. This closes the gap on the
+client side so the Runtime's structured presence records can attribute the ending session.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- The `SessionEnd` request built in `plugins/graphhelm/hooks/session_hook.py` sends
+  `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session` carrying the validated host session id, inline in the existing
+  end-request headers dict (no new header helper).
+- The existing end-request contract test in `plugins/graphhelm/hooks/test_session_hook.py`
+  (`test_end_posts_an_attributed_idempotent_observation_without_success_claim`) is extended to
+  assert the new header is present with the session id value.
+- No other changes: the `SessionStart` request, all other end-request headers, the retry/idempotency
+  behavior, and the rest of the hook test suite are untouched. No Rust, schema, or dependency changes.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `session-hooks`: wire and local-state behavior of the GraphHelm plugin's bounded SessionStart /
+  SessionEnd host hooks — specifically here, what the end (signal) request declares about the
+  acting session.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+(None — `openspec/specs/` currently holds no capabilities.)
+
+## Impact
+
+- **Code**: `plugins/graphhelm/hooks/session_hook.py` (one header added to the end-request
+  headers dict in `_end_impl`) and `plugins/graphhelm/hooks/test_session_hook.py` (assertions in
+  the one existing end-request test). Nothing else.
+- **Wire**: adds one previously-unused optional header to one existing POST. The Runtime already
+  parses and bounds `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session` (visible ASCII, ≤ 128 chars, non-blank); the
+  hook's session id is already regex-validated to at most 128 visible-ASCII characters before
+  use, so every value the hook can send is accepted by the existing Runtime bound. Runtimes or
+  servers that ignore unknown headers are unaffected (header is additive).
+- **Compatibility**: additive; **no breaking changes**. Signal bytes, idempotency keys, and
+  delivery receipts are unchanged, so stored undelivered retries behave exactly as before.
+- **Dependencies**: none added.
+- **Rollback**: revert the two files; the header disappears from the wire and the Runtime simply
+  records absence again, which it already handles.
