+# Spec Delta
+
+## Purpose
+
+Defines the wire and local-state behavior of the GraphHelm plugin's bounded SessionStart /
+SessionEnd host hooks that bridge a host coding session to a Runtime execution.
+
+## ADDED Requirements
+
+### Requirement: Session-end signal declares the host session id
+
+When a bound session ends and the hook delivers its `agent_session_ended` signal to the
+Runtime, the end request SHALL carry the `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session` header whose value is the
+host session id of the ending session. The value SHALL be the raw session id, not the composite
+actor identifier carried by `X-GraphHelm-Actor`.
+
+#### Scenario: First delivery carries the session header
+
+- **WHEN** a host ends a session bound to a GraphHelm execution and the hook posts the
+  `agent_session_ended` signal for the first time
+- **THEN** the request includes `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session` equal to that session's session id,
+  in addition to the existing actor, actor-type, and idempotency headers
+
+#### Scenario: Header value is the raw session id
+
+- **WHEN** the hook posts an end signal for host `claude` and session `session-123`
+- **THEN** `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session` is `session-123` while `X-GraphHelm-Actor` remains
+  `claude-session-session-123`
+
+#### Scenario: Retried delivery re-declares the same session
+
+- **WHEN** a previous delivery attempt was refused or lost and the hook retries the same stored
+  signal
+- **THEN** the retried request carries the same `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session` value as the
+  original, because the delivery receipt is scoped to that session
+
+### Requirement: The header addition is wire-additive
+
+Sending `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session` SHALL NOT alter any other element of the end request: the
+signal body, the idempotency key, the existing headers, or the acknowledgment match check. The
+session-start (briefing) request SHALL NOT gain this header.
+
+#### Scenario: Existing end-request elements are unchanged
+
+- **WHEN** the hook posts an end signal with the session header in place
+- **THEN** the signal body bytes, `Idempotency-Key`, `X-GraphHelm-Actor`, and
+  `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Type` are exactly as they were before the header existed, and the
+  acknowledgment is still matched on execution id and signal id
+
+#### Scenario: Start request gains no header
+
+- **WHEN** the hook reads the live briefing at session start
+- **THEN** the request does not carry `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session`
+
+### Requirement: The end-request contract test observes the header
+
+The hook's existing end-request contract test SHALL assert that the captured end request carries
+`X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session` with the session id value, and the rest of the hook test suite SHALL
+continue to pass unmodified.
+
+#### Scenario: Contract test asserts the header
+
+- **WHEN** the hook's end-request contract test runs against its in-process Runtime
+- **THEN** it asserts the captured request's `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session` equals the session id
+  used for the run
+
+#### Scenario: Remaining hook tests stay green
+
+- **WHEN** the full hook test suite is run
+- **THEN** every pre-existing test passes without modification
