+`plugins/graphhelm/hooks/test_session_hook.py`; promise: the bound `SessionEnd` signal POST
+carries `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session` set to the validated host session id, asserted by the
+existing end-request test, rest of the suite green; observation command:
+`python plugins/graphhelm/hooks/test_session_hook.py`.
+
+## 1. Contract test observes the header (red first)
+
+- [x] 1.1 Extend `test_end_posts_an_attributed_idempotent_observation_without_success_claim`
+      in `plugins/graphhelm/hooks/test_session_hook.py` to also assert
+      `sent[0][2]["X-Graphhelm-Actor-Session"] == "session-123"` — the same normalized key style
+      as the adjacent `X-Graphhelm-Actor-Type` assertion on line 186, value taken from the
+      session id the harness already uses. No changes to any other test or to
+      `RuntimeHandler`. Verify RED: run
+      `python plugins/graphhelm/hooks/test_session_hook.py SessionHookTests.test_end_posts_an_attributed_idempotent_observation_without_success_claim`
+      before touching the hook and confirm it fails on exactly this missing header.
+
+## 2. Send the header (green)
+
+- [x] 2.1 In `plugins/graphhelm/hooks/session_hook.py::_end_impl`, add
+      `"X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session": session` to the existing inline headers dict literal passed
+      to the `request(...)` end-call (the dict that already holds `X-GraphHelm-Actor`,
+      `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Type`, `Idempotency-Key`). No new helper function, no change to
+      `request()`, no change to the `SessionStart` path, no change to signal bytes or delivery
+      state. Verify GREEN: re-run the single test from 1.1 and confirm it passes.
+
+## 3. Boundary checks
+
+- [x] 3.1 Run the full hook suite: `python plugins/graphhelm/hooks/test_session_hook.py` and
+      confirm every pre-existing test passes unmodified (baseline at plan time: 26 tests OK on
+      Python 3.11.9).
+- [x] 3.2 Confirm the start request stays header-free and the diff is contained: review
+      `git diff --stat` — only `plugins/graphhelm/hooks/session_hook.py`,
+      `plugins/graphhelm/hooks/test_session_hook.py` (plus `openspec/changes/bench-feature/`)
+      changed; the hook diff adds exactly one dict entry and the test diff adds assertions to
+      the one named test.
